# Per-host kanata deduplication. Active on rgx1gen11 only; other hosts
# get the empty header below.
#
# Problem: kanata grabs the built-in keyboard via evdev and emits its
# transformed (Colemak + Extend + AltGr-Icelandic) stream via a uinput
# virtual device. On rgx1gen11 the exclusive grab does not always hold,
# and sway sees BOTH devices as active keyboards:
#
#   1:1:AT_Translated_Set_2_keyboard    (physical, QWERTY scancodes)
#   1:1:kanata                          (virtual, Colemak scancodes)
#
# Result: every keypress is delivered twice, so $mod+Return opens two
# terminals, $mod+Shift+q sends two close events, etc.
#
# Fix: disable libinput events from the physical device. Kanata still
# reads it (evdev, a layer below libinput) so the Colemak remap is
# unaffected; sway only hears kanata's transformed output.
#
# If kanata dies or is disabled, *typing stops working on the internal
# keyboard*. Recovery: any external USB keyboard still works (different
# device ID), or Alt+SysRq+K emergencies plus the sway bind to start
# foot, or drop to TTY. Trade-off accepted -- doubled keys are more
# disruptive day-to-day than a kanata-down scenario that has its own
# alarms (no Colemak = immediately obvious).
{{- if eq .chezmoi.hostname "rgx1gen11" }}

input "1:1:AT_Translated_Set_2_keyboard" {
    events disabled
}
{{- end }}
